## Overview

The pointer tagging system is a critical part of the V8/Zig FFI boundary but is currently undocumented. This creates confusion and bugs \(like the segfault we're fixing\).

## Documentation Locations

### 1. Update pointer_tag.zig header comment
```zig
//\! # Pointer Tagging System
//\!
//\! This module implements a pointer tagging scheme to distinguish between
//\! different types of opaque pointers at the V8/Zig boundary.
//\!
//\! ## Why Tagging?
//\!
//\! When converting V8 values to Zig, we often use `*const anyopaque` to
//\! represent values whose concrete type isn't known at compile time.
//\! Tagging allows us to distinguish:
//\! - V8 Global handles \(persistent, need explicit release\)
//\! - V8 Local handles \(temporary, scope-managed\)
//\! - Zig runtime instances \(our allocated objects\)
//\!
//\! ## Tag Values
//\!
//\! The low 2 bits of the pointer encode the type:
//\! - 0b00 \(.untagged\): Legacy/untagged pointer
//\! - 0b01 \(.global_handle\): V8 Global\<Value\> handle
//\! - 0b10 \(.runtime_instance\): Zig-allocated runtime.Instance
//\! - 0b11 \(.local_value\): V8 Local\<Value\> handle
//\!
//\! ## Usage Contract
//\!
//\! **Producers** \(code that creates tagged pointers\):
//\! - `fromV8Value` in conversions.zig tags `*const anyopaque` values
//\! - Tag is chosen based on value type detection
//\!
//\! **Consumers** \(code that uses tagged pointers\):
//\! - MUST call `untagPointer\(\)` before passing to V8 FFI
//\! - MAY use tag to determine how to handle the value
//\! - MUST NOT use `@alignCast` on tagged pointers
//\!
//\! ## Example
//\!
//\! ```zig
//\! // Receiving a potentially tagged pointer
//\! fn processValue\(value: *const anyopaque\) void {
//\!     const untagged = untagPointer\(value\)\;
//\!     
//\!     switch \(untagged.tag\) {
//\!         .runtime_instance =\> {
//\!             // It's a Zig object, can cast to Instance
//\!             const instance: *runtime.Instance = @ptrCast\(untagged.ptr\)\;
//\!         },
//\!         .global_handle, .local_value =\> {
//\!             // It's a V8 handle, pass to FFI
//\!             const v8_value: *ffi.Value = @ptrCast\(untagged.ptr\)\;
//\!             ffi.v8_SomeFunction\(v8_value\)\;
//\!         },
//\!         .untagged =\> {
//\!             // Legacy code, treat as V8 value
//\!         },
//\!     }
//\! }
//\! ```
```

