### Scheme Fetch
```zig
/// Scheme fetch - dispatch based on URL scheme.
///
/// Algorithm:
/// 1. If fetchParams is canceled, return appropriate network error
/// 2. Let request be fetchParams's request
/// 3. Switch on request's current URL's scheme:
///
///    "about":
///    - If request URL is about:blank, return response with 
///      status 200, header (Content-Type, text/html;charset=utf-8), body empty
///    - Return network error
///
///    "blob":
///    - Resolve blob URL
///    - If fails, return network error
///    - Return response with blob data
///
///    "data":
///    - Let dataURLResult = data URL processor on request URL
///    - If failure, return network error
///    - Return response with status 200, header Content-Type = mimeType, body
///
///    "file":
///    - Implementation-defined (return network error for now)
///
///    "http" or "https":
///    - Return result of HTTP fetch
///
///    Otherwise:
///    - Return network error
pub fn schemeFetch(
    allocator: std.mem.Allocator,
    fetch_params: *FetchParams,
    network_backend: *NetworkBackend,
    cache_backend: *CacheBackend,
) !*InternalResponse {
    if (fetch_params.isCanceled()) {
        return createAppropriateNetworkError(allocator, fetch_params);
    }

    const request = fetch_params.request;
    const scheme = request.currentUrl().scheme;

    if (std.mem.eql(u8, scheme, "about")) {
        return aboutFetch(allocator, request);
    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, scheme, "blob")) {
        return blobFetch(allocator, request);
    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, scheme, "data")) {
        return dataFetch(allocator, request);
    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, scheme, "file")) {
        // Implementation-defined
        return InternalResponse.networkError(allocator);
    } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, scheme, "http") or 
               std.mem.eql(u8, scheme, "https")) {
        return httpFetch(allocator, fetch_params, network_backend, cache_backend);
    } else {
        return InternalResponse.networkError(allocator);
    }
}
```

