## Background
Once dependencies are added to build.zig.zon, we need build.zig logic to:
1. Fetch the curl dependency with correct options
2. Configure mbedTLS as TLS backend
3. Disable unused features to minimize binary size
4. Link the static library to the fetch module
5. Add required macros and platform-specific libraries

## Implementation

### Main Function
```zig
/// Configure statically-compiled libcurl for the fetch module
///
/// Compiles libcurl from source using allyourcodebase/curl package.
/// TLS provided by mbedTLS (cross-platform, no system dependencies).
///
/// Features enabled:
/// - HTTP/HTTPS (with mbedTLS)
/// - Compression (gzip via zlib)
///
/// Features disabled (minimize binary size):
/// - LDAP, LDAPS (not needed for Fetch)
/// - libpsl (Public Suffix List)
/// - libssh2 (SSH/SCP/SFTP)
/// - libidn2 (IDN - URL module handles IDNA)
/// - nghttp2 (HTTP/2 - optional, can enable later)
/// - brotli, zstd (additional compression)
fn configureStaticLibcurl(
    b: *std.Build,
    module: *std.Build.Module,
    target: std.Build.ResolvedTarget,
    optimize: std.builtin.OptimizeMode,
) void {
    const curl_dep = b.lazyDependency("curl", .{
        .target = target,
        .optimize = optimize,
        .linkage = .static,
        // TLS backend
        .@"use-openssl" = false,
        .@"use-mbedtls" = true,
        .@"use-schannel" = false,
        // Disable optional dependencies
        .libpsl = false,
        .libssh2 = false,
        .libidn2 = false,
        .nghttp2 = false,
        .@"disable-ldap" = true,
        .brotli = false,
        .zstd = false,
    }) orelse {
        @panic("curl dependency not available");
    };

    // Get static library artifact
    const libcurl = @import("curl").artifact(curl_dep, .lib);

    // Link to module
    module.linkLibrary(libcurl);

    // Required for static linking
    module.addCMacro("CURL_STATICLIB", "1");

    // Platform-specific system libraries
    const os = target.result.os.tag;
    if (os == .windows) {
        module.linkSystemLibrary("ws2_32", .{});
        module.linkSystemLibrary("bcrypt", .{});
        module.linkSystemLibrary("advapi32", .{});
        module.linkSystemLibrary("crypt32", .{});
    } else if (os == .linux) {
        module.linkSystemLibrary("pthread", .{});
    }
    // macOS: no additional libraries needed with mbedTLS
}
```

