Implement body cloning using ReadableStream.tee().

## Spec Reference
- https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-body-clone
- specs/whatwg/fetch.md (line 757-764)

## Location
`src/fetch/body/cloning.zig`

## Requirements

### Clone Body Algorithm
```zig
/// Clone a body.
///
/// Spec Algorithm:
/// 1. Let (out1, out2) = tee(body's stream)
/// 2. Set body's stream to out1
/// 3. Return a body whose stream is out2 and other members are copied from body
///
/// This allows both the original body and the clone to be read independently.
pub fn cloneBody(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, body: *Body) !*Body {
    // Step 1: Tee the stream
    const tee_result = try body.stream.tee();

    // Step 2: Set original body's stream to first branch
    body.stream = tee_result.branch1;

    // Step 3: Create new body with second branch
    const cloned_body = try allocator.create(Body);
    cloned_body.* = .{
        .allocator = allocator,
        .stream = tee_result.branch2,
        .source = body.source,  // Copy source reference
        .length = body.length,  // Copy length
    };

    return cloned_body;
}
```

### Clone for Request
```zig
/// Clone request's body for Request.clone().
/// If body is null, cloned request also has null body.
pub fn cloneRequestBody(
    allocator: std.mem.Allocator, 
    request: *InternalRequest
) !?*Body {
    if (request.body) |body| {
        return switch (body) {
            .bytes => |b| try Body.fromBytes(allocator, b),
            .body => |b| try cloneBody(allocator, b),
        };
    }
    return null;
}
```

### Clone for Response
