## Summary

When the parser encounters `\<script src="..."\>`, it needs to:
1. Pause parsing \(for blocking scripts\)
2. Fetch the external script
3. Execute the script
4. Resume parsing

## Spec Reference

HTML Standard § 4.12.1.1 Processing model
- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#script-processing-model

## Script Types

### Parser-blocking scripts \(default\)
- `\<script src="..."\>\</script\>`
- Parser must wait for fetch and execution

### Async scripts
- `\<script src="..." async\>\</script\>`
- Parser continues, script executes when ready

### Deferred scripts
- `\<script src="..." defer\>\</script\>`
- Parser continues, script executes after parsing complete

### Module scripts
- `\<script type="module" src="..."\>\</script\>`
- Always deferred by default

## Implementation

### 1. Script Fetch Context

```zig
pub const ScriptFetchContext = struct {
    allocator: Allocator,
    parser: *TreeBuilder,
    script_element: *runtime.Instance,
    script_type: ScriptType,
    url: []const u8,

    pub const ScriptType = enum {
        classic_blocking,
        classic_async,
        classic_defer,
        module,
    }\;
}\;
```

### 2. WPT Runner Script Loading

For WPT tests, scripts are local files:

```zig
fn loadExternalScript\(ctx: *ParserScriptContext, src: []const u8\) \![]const u8 {
    // Resolve relative to test file
    const script_path = try resolvePath\(ctx.base_url, src\)\;

    // Read from WPT directory
    const content = try std.fs.cwd\(\).readFileAlloc\(ctx.allocator, script_path, max_script_size\)\;

    return content\;
}
```

### 3. Parser-Blocking Flow

```zig
fn handleExternalScript\(ctx: *ParserScriptContext, script_node: *TreeNode\) \!void {
    const src = getScriptSrc\(script_node\) orelse return\;
    const is_async = hasAttribute\(script_node, "async"\)\;
    const is_defer = hasAttribute\(script_node, "defer"\)\;

    if \(is_async\) {
        // Queue for async execution
        try ctx.async_scripts.append\(.{
            .url = src,
            .script_element = ctx.dom_adapter.getDomNode\(script_node\),
        }\)\;
        return\; // Parser continues
    }

    if \(is_defer\) {
        // Queue for deferred execution
        try ctx.defer_scripts.append\(.{
            .url = src,
            .script_element = ctx.dom_adapter.getDomNode\(script_node\),
        }\)\;
        return\; // Parser continues
    }

    // Parser-blocking: fetch and execute now
    const content = try loadExternalScript\(ctx, src\)\;
    defer ctx.allocator.free\(content\)\;

    try executeScript\(ctx, content\)\;
}
```

### 4. Deferred Script Execution

After parsing completes:

```zig
fn executeDeferredScripts\(ctx: *ParserScriptContext\) \!void {
    for \(ctx.defer_scripts.items\) \|script_info\| {
        const content = try loadExternalScript\(ctx, script_info.url\)\;
        defer ctx.allocator.free\(content\)\;
        try executeScript\(ctx, content\)\;
    }
}
```

