## Overview

Add debug-mode assertions at V8 FFI boundaries to catch incorrect pointer usage early. This helps prevent subtle bugs where tagged pointers are passed to V8 or untagged pointers are used where tagged ones are expected.

## Assertion Points

### 1. Before V8 FFI calls
```zig
pub fn callV8Function\(ptr: *anyopaque\) void {
    if \(builtin.mode == .Debug\) {
        // Ensure we're not passing a tagged pointer to V8
        const tag = TaggedPointer.fromRaw\(@intFromPtr\(ptr\)\).getTag\(\)\;
        if \(tag \!= .untagged\) {
            std.debug.panic\("Tagged pointer {any} passed to V8 FFI", .{tag}\)\;
        }
    }
    // ... actual call
}
```

### 2. After V8 returns pointers
```zig
pub fn getV8Handle\(\) TaggedPointer {
    const raw = v8.getHandle\(\)\;
    if \(builtin.mode == .Debug\) {
        // V8 should return aligned pointers
        std.debug.assert\(@intFromPtr\(raw\) \& 0b11 == 0\)\;
    }
    return TaggedPointer.init\(raw, .global_handle\)\;
}
```

### 3. At conversion boundaries
```zig
pub fn fromV8Value\(value: *v8.Value\) TaggedPointer {
    if \(builtin.mode == .Debug\) {
        // Log for debugging
        std.log.debug\("Creating tagged pointer: {x} tag={}", .{
            @intFromPtr\(value\),
            TaggedPointer.Tag.local_value,
        }\)\;
    }
    return TaggedPointer.init\(@ptrCast\(value\), .local_value\)\;
}
```

## Assertion Helper Functions

```zig
pub const DebugAssertions = struct {
    pub fn assertNotTagged\(ptr: *const anyopaque\) void {
        if \(builtin.mode == .Debug\) {
            const addr = @intFromPtr\(ptr\)\;
            if \(addr \& 0b11 \!= 0\) {
                std.debug.panic\(
                    "Expected untagged pointer, got tagged: {x} \(tag bits: {b}\)",
                    .{ addr, addr \& 0b11 }
                \)\;
            }
        }
    }

    pub fn assertTagged\(ptr: *const anyopaque, expected: TaggedPointer.Tag\) void {
        if \(builtin.mode == .Debug\) {
            const actual = TaggedPointer.fromRaw\(@intFromPtr\(ptr\)\).getTag\(\)\;
            if \(actual \!= expected\) {
                std.debug.panic\(
                    "Expected tag {}, got {}",
                    .{ expected, actual }
                \)\;
            }
        }
    }
}\;
```

