## Overview

When V8 converts JavaScript objects to Zig dictionaries, interface-typed members \(like `ReadableWritablePair.writable`\) are stored as raw `*v8.Value` pointers via the `*const anyopaque` branch. The code that uses these values incorrectly assumes they are `*runtime.Instance` pointers.

## Current Behavior \(BROKEN\)

In `src/runtime/engines/v8/conversions.zig` \(lines 928-938\):
```zig
if \(T == *const anyopaque\) {
    // For anyopaque parameters \(WebIDL 'any' type\), pass through the V8 value as-is.
    // The V8 value pointer \(Global\<Value\>*\) is returned so it can be stored and
    // passed back to JavaScript unchanged.
    return @ptrCast\(value\)\;  // Returns V8 Value*, NOT runtime.Instance\!
}
```

In `src/webidl/impls/ReadableStream.zig` \(line 788\):
```zig
const writable: *runtime.Instance = @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(@constCast\(transform.writable\)\)\)\;
// ^^^ WRONG: transform.writable is a *v8.Value, not *runtime.Instance\!
```

## Required Fix

### Option A: Fix at Conversion Site \(Preferred\)

Modify `fromV8Value` to detect when `T == *const anyopaque` but the V8 value is actually a wrapped object with internal fields. If internal fields exist, extract the `*runtime.Instance`:

```zig
if \(T == *const anyopaque\) {
    // Check if this is a wrapped Zig object
    if \(value.isObject\(\)\) {
        const obj = value.toObject\(context\) orelse return @ptrCast\(value\)\;
        if \(obj.internalFieldCount\(\) \> 0\) {
            // Extract the runtime.Instance from internal field
            const internal = obj.getInternalField\(0\)\;
            if \(\!internal.isUndefined\(\)\) {
                return @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(internal.toExternal\(\)\)\)\;
            }
        }
    }
    // Fall back to raw V8 value for true 'any' types
    return @ptrCast\(value\)\;
}
```

### Option B: Fix at Usage Site

Create a helper function in `ReadableStream.zig`:

```zig
fn unwrapV8Instance\(v8_ptr: *const anyopaque, comptime InterfaceType: type\) \!*runtime.Instance {
    const value: *v8.Value = @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(@constCast\(v8_ptr\)\)\)\;
    const obj = value.toObject\(context\) orelse return error.InvalidValue\;
    const internal = obj.getInternalField\(0\)\;
    // ... extract and validate instance
}
```

