## Overview

Add defensive validation helpers to catch V8 pointer type confusion early with better error messages.

## Problem

When V8 pointers are misused \(Local passed where Global expected\), the result is cryptic "misaligned address" errors.

## Solution

### C++ Validation \(v8_wrapper.cpp\)

```cpp
extern "C" bool v8_ValidateGlobalPointer\(void* ptr\) {
    uintptr_t addr = reinterpret_cast\<uintptr_t\>\(ptr\)\;
    if \(addr \< 0x1000\) return false\;  // Null page
    if \(addr \& 0x7\) return false\;      // Misaligned
    if \(\(addr \& 0x1\) == 1\) return false\;  // V8 tagged pointer
    return true\;
}
```

### Zig Validation \(validation.zig\)

```zig
pub fn validateV8Pointer\(ptr: *const anyopaque, comptime context: []const u8\) \!void {
    const addr = @intFromPtr\(ptr\)\;
    if \(\(addr \& 0x1\) == 1\) {
        std.debug.print\("[V8 ERROR] {s}: tagged V8 pointer passed where Global expected\n", .{context}\)\;
        return error.V8TaggedPointer\;
    }
}
```

