## Summary

TransformStream's callback extraction code doesn't account for the pointer tagging system used throughout the codebase. When receiving a `*const anyopaque` parameter, it should untag the pointer before using it with V8 APIs.

## Background: Pointer Tagging System

The codebase uses 2-bit pointer tagging defined in `src/runtime/engines/v8/pointer_tag.zig`:

```zig
pub const PointerTag = enum\(u2\) {
    untagged = 0,        // 00 - No tag, legacy pointer
    global_handle = 1,   // 01 - V8 Global handle
    runtime_instance = 2,// 10 - Zig runtime.Instance
    local_value = 3,     // 11 - V8 Local handle
}\;
```

## Current Code \(Missing Untag\)

**File**: `src/webidl/impls/TransformStream.zig:450-461`

```zig
// Line 452: No untagging\!
const v8_obj: *v8.Object = @ptrCast\(@constCast\(transformer\)\)\;

// Line 461: Uses potentially tagged pointer with V8
if \(v8.v8_Object_Get\(v8_obj, v8_context, @ptrCast\(transform_key\)\)\) \|transform_val\| {
```

## Required Fix

Add proper untagging before use:

```zig
const pointer_tag = @import\("../../runtime/engines/v8/pointer_tag.zig"\)\;

fn setUpTransformStreamDefaultControllerFromTransformer\(
    // ...
    transformer: *const anyopaque,
\) \!void {
    // Untag the pointer to get raw pointer and tag info
    const untagged = pointer_tag.untagPointer\(@ptrCast\(transformer\)\)\;

    switch \(untagged.tag\) {
        .global_handle =\> {
            // This is a V8 Global handle - use directly with V8 FFI
            const v8_obj: *v8.Object = @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(untagged.ptr\)\)\;
            // ... extract callbacks using v8_Object_Get ...
        },
        .local_value =\> {
            // This is a V8 Local handle - may need special handling
            // Local handles are only valid within their HandleScope
            const v8_val: *v8.Value = @ptrCast\(untagged.ptr\)\;
            if \(v8.v8_Value_IsObject\(v8_val\)\) {
                const v8_obj = v8.v8_Value_ToObject\(v8_val, v8_context\) orelse {
                    // Conversion failed - use default algorithms
                    return\;
                }\;
                // ... extract callbacks ...
            }
        },
        .runtime_instance =\> {
            // This is a Zig runtime.Instance, NOT a V8 object\!
            // Cannot extract JavaScript callbacks - use default algorithms
            controller_state.own._internal = controller_internal\;
            internal.controller = controller\;
            return\;
        },
        .untagged =\> {
            // Legacy untagged pointer - need additional validation
            // Check alignment and validate before use
            const addr = @intFromPtr\(untagged.ptr\)\;
            if \(addr % 8 \!= 0\) {
                // Misaligned - not a valid V8 Global handle
                controller_state.own._internal = controller_internal\;
                internal.controller = controller\;
                return\;
            }
            // Assume it's a V8 object \(legacy behavior\)
            const v8_obj: *v8.Object = @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(untagged.ptr\)\)\;
            // ... extract callbacks ...
        },
    }
}
```

## Why This Matters

The `fromV8Value` function in `conversions.zig` may return tagged pointers. When `*const anyopaque` values flow through the system, they may have any of the 4 tag values. Using a tagged pointer directly with V8 FFI functions will cause misalignment errors or worse.

