Worker context WPT tests fail with "TypeError: number 791666112 is not a function" because when JavaScript accesses properties stored as Global handles \(like `message.data`\), we return the raw `Global\<Value\>*` C++ pointer instead of converting it to a `Local\<Value\>` that V8 can use.

## Fixes Implemented

### Fix 1: conversions.zig toV8Value \(whatwg-phakw\) ✅
Changed the `.handle` case to convert Global handles to Local:
```zig
.handle =\> \|h\| blk: {
    if \(h.handle_scope == .global\) {
        const local = v8.v8_Global_Get\(isolate, @ptrCast\(h.ptr\)\)\;
        break :blk if \(local\) \|l\| @ptrCast\(l\) else toV8Undefined\(isolate\)\;
