## Spec Notes

### Byte Stream Controller
- Use ReadableByteStreamController (type: "bytes") for efficient byte-level access
- Enables BYOB (Bring Your Own Buffer) reads for zero-copy when possible

### Chunk Size
- Spec doesn't define chunk size, implementation-defined
- 64KB is reasonable default (matches many I/O buffer sizes)

### Error Handling
- If chunk read fails, error the stream with appropriate DOMException
- NotReadableError for general read failures
- NotFoundError if underlying file was deleted (for File objects)

### Task Queuing
- Per spec, chunks should be enqueued via "file reading task source"
- In practice, this means async scheduling through event loop

