### Extract Body
```zig
/// Extract a body and Content-Type from a BodyInit.
///
/// Algorithm:
/// 1. Let stream = null, action = null, source = null, length = null, type = null
/// 2. Switch on object:
///    - ReadableStream: set stream to object
///    - Blob: set source to object, length to size, 
///            action = read from blob, type = blob.type if non-empty
///    - BufferSource: set source to copy of bytes, length to byte length
///    - FormData: set action = multipart/form-data encode,
///               source = object, length = ?, type = multipart/form-data;boundary=...
///    - URLSearchParams: set source to urlencoded serialize,
///               length = ?, type = application/x-www-form-urlencoded;charset=UTF-8
///    - String (USVString): set source to UTF-8 encode,
///               length = byte length, type = text/plain;charset=UTF-8
/// 3. If source is byte sequence, set stream to ReadableStream from source
/// 4. If action is non-null, set stream to ReadableStream with pull = action
/// 5. Return ((stream, source, length), type)
pub fn extract(allocator: std.mem.Allocator, object: BodyInit) !BodyWithType
```

