## Implementation

Per HTML spec, `document.title` should:
1. For HTML documents: Return the text content of the first `\<title\>` element
2. For SVG documents: Return the text content of the first `\<title\>` child of SVG root
3. Strip and collapse whitespace

```zig
pub fn get_title\(instance: *Instance\) \![]const u8 {
    const doc = getDocument\(instance\)\;

    // Find first \<title\> element in document
    if \(doc.getElementsByTagName\("title"\)\) \|titles\| {
        if \(titles.length\(\) \> 0\) {
            const title_elem = titles.item\(0\)\;
            const text = title_elem.textContent orelse ""\;
            return stripAndCollapseWhitespace\(text\)\;
        }
    }
    return ""\;
}
```

