/// Parse a WebSocket frame header from raw bytes.
///
/// This function implements RFC 6455 Section 5.2 (Base Framing Protocol).
///
/// ## Arguments
/// - `data`: Raw bytes containing the frame header (minimum 2 bytes)
/// - `is_client`: True if we're the client receiving from server
///
/// ## Returns
/// A struct containing:
/// - `header`: The parsed FrameHeader
/// - `bytes_consumed`: Number of bytes used for the header
///
/// ## Errors
/// - `Incomplete`: Not enough bytes to parse header
/// - `ReservedBitsSet`: RSV bits set without extension
/// - `ControlFrameTooLarge`: Control frame > 125 bytes
/// - `FragmentedControlFrame`: Control frame with FIN=0
///
