## Summary

All algorithm vtables in common.zig use `ptr: *anyopaque` for context passing. This loses type information and enables unsafe casts.

## Current Code \(common.zig:452-457\)

```zig
pub const StartAlgorithm = struct {
    ptr: *anyopaque,
    vtable: *const VTable,

    pub const VTable = struct {
        call: *const fn \(ctx: *anyopaque\) Promise\(void\),
        deinit: ?*const fn \(ctx: *anyopaque\) void,
    }\;
    // ...
}\;
```

This pattern repeats for: StartAlgorithm, PullAlgorithm, CancelAlgorithm, SizeAlgorithm, WriteAlgorithm, CloseAlgorithm, AbortAlgorithm, FlushAlgorithm, TransformAlgorithm, AsyncIterator.

## Solution

Create a generic TypedContext system:

```zig
/// Generic algorithm with compile-time known context type
pub fn GenericAlgorithm\(comptime Context: type, comptime Result: type\) type {
    return struct {
        context: *Context,
        call_fn: *const fn \(*Context\) Result,
        deinit_fn: ?*const fn \(*Context\) void,

        pub fn call\(self: @This\(\)\) Result {
            return self.call_fn\(self.context\)\;
        }

        pub fn deinit\(self: @This\(\)\) void {
            if \(self.deinit_fn\) \|f\| f\(self.context\)\;
        }
    }\;
}

// Type-erased wrapper for runtime polymorphism when needed
pub const ErasedAlgorithm = struct {
    ptr: *anyopaque,
    type_id: TypeId,  // Runtime type tag
    vtable: *const VTable,
}\;
```

