## Task

Refactor GC integration code and tests to use typed patterns instead of anyopaque casts.

## Current Pattern

```zig
// src/runtime/gc_integration.zig:84
pub fn onObjectFreed\(user_data: ?*anyopaque\) callconv\(.c\) void {
    const inst = @as\(*Instance, @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(user_data orelse return\)\)\)\;
    // ...
}

// tests/runtime/gc_integration.zig:41
instance.state == @as\(*anyopaque, @ptrCast\(state\)\)
```

## Analysis

GC callbacks have `callconv\(.c\)` which requires anyopaque for C ABI compatibility. However:
1. The callback wrapper pattern can hide the anyopaque from user code
2. Type assertions can be added for safety
3. Test code can use typed comparisons

## Proposed Pattern

```zig
// Typed GC callback wrapper
pub fn TypedGCCallback\(comptime T: type\) type {
    return struct {
        pub fn wrap\(typed_callback: *const fn \(*T\) void\) GCCallback {
            return struct {
                fn callback\(user_data: ?*anyopaque\) callconv\(.c\) void {
                    const typed = @as\(*T, @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(user_data orelse return\)\)\)\;
                    typed_callback\(typed\)\;
                }
            }.callback\;
        }
    }\;
}

// Test comparisons
try testing.expectEqual\(instance.getTypedState\(StateType\), expected_state\)\;
```

