\| 3160 \| `@ptrCast\(@alignCast\(@constCast\(...\)\)\)` \| `removeAttributeNode\(\)` \|

## Problem

These functions receive variadic arguments \(`...nodes`\) or single element parameters from JavaScript. When converted, they're tagged pointers.

## Fix Pattern

For each location:

```zig
// BEFORE:
const v8_node: *v8.Object = @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(@constCast\(nodes\)\)\)\;

// AFTER:
const pointer_tag = @import\("v8"\).pointer_tag\;
const untagged = pointer_tag.untagPointer\(nodes\)\;

// For DOM operations, we might actually WANT runtime_instance
// \(if it's a Zig-backed Node\)
switch \(untagged.tag\) {
    .runtime_instance =\> {
        // This IS a Zig Node instance - use directly
        const node: *Node = @ptrCast\(@alignCast\(untagged.ptr\)\)\;
        // ... use node
    },
    .global_handle, .local_value, .untagged =\> {
        // This is a V8 object - extract internal field
        const v8_obj: *v8.Object = @ptrCast\(untagged.ptr\)\;
        // ... get internal Node from v8_obj
    },
}
```

