## Overview

Ensure interface bindings \(constructors, prototypes\) are registered separately for each V8 context. This is required for cross-realm instanceof to work correctly.

## Current State

`src/runtime/engines/v8/interface_bindings.zig` registers all interfaces on a context, but the template registry may be shared.

## Key Insight

For cross-realm to work, each context needs:
- Its own `Element.prototype` \(so `mainDoc.body instanceof iframe.Element` returns false\)
- Its own `TypeError` constructor \(for throwing from correct realm\)
- Its own interface constructor functions

## Required Changes

### 1. Review Template Registry

```zig
// Current: template_registry.zig may cache templates globally
// Need: Templates can be shared \(they're like classes\)
// BUT: Instances \(prototypes, constructors\) must be per-context

// V8 FunctionTemplate is like a blueprint - can be shared
// v8.v8_FunctionTemplate_GetFunction\(\) returns a Function - this is per-context
```

### 2. Ensure Per-Context Registration

```zig
// In interface_bindings.zig

/// Initialize all bindings for a new context
pub fn initializeBindings\(isolate: v8.Isolate, context: v8.Context\) \!void {
    // Enter context to ensure all operations use this context
    v8.v8_Context_Enter\(context\)\;
    defer v8.v8_Context_Exit\(context\)\;

    // Register all interfaces - each call creates NEW constructor/prototype
    // in the current context
    try registerAllInterfaces\(isolate, context\)\;

    // Set up inheritance relationships in THIS context
    try setupConstructorInheritance\(isolate, context\)\;

    // Register legacy factory functions \(Image, Audio, Option\)
    try registerLegacyFactoryFunctions\(isolate, context\)\;

    // Register namespaces
    try registerAllNamespaces\(isolate, context\)\;
}

/// Register a single interface's constructor on the global object
pub fn registerInterface\(
    comptime Interface: type,
    isolate: v8.Isolate,
    context: v8.Context,
\) \!void {
    const global = v8.v8_Context_Global\(context\)\;

    // Get or create template \(can be cached\)
    const template = V8Interface\(Interface\).getTemplate\(isolate\)\;

    // Get function FROM this context - this is per-context\!
    const constructor = v8.v8_FunctionTemplate_GetFunction\(context, template\)\;

    // Define on this context's global object
    const name = v8.v8_String_NewFromUtf8\(isolate, Interface.name\)\;
    v8.v8_Object_DefineProperty\(global, name, .{
        .value = constructor,
        .writable = true,
        .enumerable = false,
        .configurable = true,
    }\)\;
}
```

### 3. Verify Prototype Separation

```zig
// Test that prototypes are truly separate
test "interface prototypes are per-context" {
    const isolate = v8.createIsolate\(\)\;

    // Create two contexts
    const ctx1 = v8.v8_Context_New\(isolate\)\;
    const ctx2 = v8.v8_Context_New\(isolate\)\;

    // Initialize bindings in both
    try initializeBindings\(isolate, ctx1\)\;
    try initializeBindings\(isolate, ctx2\)\;

    // Get Element.prototype from each
    v8.v8_Context_Enter\(ctx1\)\;
    const proto1 = getElementPrototype\(isolate, ctx1\)\;
    v8.v8_Context_Exit\(ctx1\)\;

    v8.v8_Context_Enter\(ctx2\)\;
    const proto2 = getElementPrototype\(isolate, ctx2\)\;
    v8.v8_Context_Exit\(ctx2\)\;

    // They should be different objects\!
    try testing.expect\(proto1 \!= proto2\)\;
    try testing.expect\(\!v8.v8_Value_StrictEquals\(proto1, proto2\)\)\;
}
```

### 4. Verify Cross-Realm instanceof

```zig
test "cross-realm instanceof returns false" {
    // Create element in context 1
    v8.v8_Context_Enter\(ctx1\)\;
    const element = createElement\(isolate, ctx1, "div"\)\;
    v8.v8_Context_Exit\(ctx1\)\;

