## Problem
Even with the poll\(\) fix, if something goes wrong the event loop can still spin at 100% CPU. We need a safety mechanism.

## Solution
Add exponential backoff when poll\(\) returns false repeatedly:
1. Track consecutive poll\(\) calls that return false \(no work done\)
2. After N consecutive "no work" polls, introduce a small sleep
3. Increase sleep duration exponentially up to a maximum
4. Reset backoff counter when poll\(\) returns true \(work was done\)

## Proposed Implementation
```zig
const BACKOFF_THRESHOLD = 10\;  // Start backoff after 10 empty polls
const MAX_BACKOFF_MS = 100\;    // Cap at 100ms

var empty_poll_count: u32 = 0\;

fn pollWithBackoff\(self: *Self\) bool {
    const did_work = self.poll\(\)\;
    if \(did_work\) {
        empty_poll_count = 0\;
        return true\;
    }

    empty_poll_count += 1\;
    if \(empty_poll_count \> BACKOFF_THRESHOLD\) {
        const backoff_ms = @min\(MAX_BACKOFF_MS, 1 \<\< \(empty_poll_count - BACKOFF_THRESHOLD\)\)\;
        std.time.sleep\(backoff_ms * std.time.ns_per_ms\)\;
    }
    return false\;
}
```

