## Overview

Verify that `instanceof` returns `false` when checking a platform object against a constructor from a different realm. This should work automatically if interface bindings are correctly separated per-context.

## WPT Test Requirements

From `has-instance.html`:
```javascript
// Same-realm instanceof works based on prototype chain
var obj = Object.create\(Element.prototype\)\;
assert_true\(obj instanceof Element\)\;
assert_true\(obj instanceof Node\)\;

// Cross-realm instanceof must return FALSE
assert_false\(document.body instanceof frames[0].Element\)\;

// Platform objects should NOT have custom Symbol.hasInstance
assert_false\(EventTarget.hasOwnProperty\(Symbol.hasInstance\)\)\;
```

## Expected Behavior

Cross-realm instanceof should return false because:
1. `document.body.[[Prototype]]` chains to `mainWindow.Element.prototype`
2. `frames[0].Element.prototype` is a DIFFERENT object
3. Standard instanceof walks prototype chain and doesn't find it

```
document.body → HTMLBodyElement.prototype \(main\)
              → HTMLElement.prototype \(main\)
              → Element.prototype \(main\) ← NOT frames[0].Element.prototype
              → Node.prototype \(main\)
              → EventTarget.prototype \(main\)
              → Object.prototype \(main\)

frames[0].Element.prototype is a separate object in frames[0]'s context
```

## Required Verification

### 1. No Custom @@hasInstance

Ensure platform object constructors do NOT have a custom `Symbol.hasInstance`:

```zig
// In interface.zig - when creating constructor

// DON'T do this:
// v8.v8_Object_Set\(constructor, symbol_hasInstance, customHasInstance\)\;

// Standard behavior is correct:
// - V8's built-in instanceof walks [[Prototype]] chain
// - No custom Symbol.hasInstance means standard behavior
```

### 2. Verify Prototype Separation

