## Problem

Internal JavaScript scripts use `self.xxx = ...` but `globalThis.xxx = ...` would be more robust since `globalThis` is always defined in V8, regardless of initialization order.

## Location

`tests/wpt_runner/browser_context.zig` - JavaScript string literals around lines 581, 612, 630

## Current Code

```javascript
// Console script \(~line 581\)
self.console = { log: ..., error: ..., ... }\;

// btoa/atob script \(~line 612\)
self.btoa = function\(str\) { ... }\;
self.atob = function\(str\) { ... }\;

// TextEncoder script \(~line 630\)
self.TextEncoder = class { ... }\;
self.TextDecoder = class { ... }\;
```

## Fix

Replace `self` with `globalThis`:

```javascript
// Console script
globalThis.console = { log: ..., error: ..., ... }\;

// btoa/atob script
globalThis.btoa = function\(str\) { ... }\;
globalThis.atob = function\(str\) { ... }\;

// TextEncoder script
globalThis.TextEncoder = class { ... }\;
globalThis.TextDecoder = class { ... }\;
```

## Rationale

- `globalThis` is always defined in V8 contexts \(ES2020 standard\)
- `self` is only defined after we explicitly set it in `setupGlobalAliases\(\)`
- Using `globalThis` makes these scripts independent of initialization order
- This is a defense-in-depth fix \(primary fix is reordering initialization\)

## Verification

Scripts should work regardless of when `setupGlobalAliases\(\)` is called.

