## Background
Per WHATWG Fetch spec section 4.8, CORS preflight:
1. Sends OPTIONS request with CORS headers
2. Validates response headers
3. Caches successful preflight results
4. Currently uses mock/stubbed network

## Current State
- Preflight generation exists at `src/fetch/cors/preflight.zig`
- Preflight cache exists at `src/fetch/cors/preflight_cache.zig`
- No actual network request for preflight

## Implementation

### Update CORS preflight to use network
```zig
pub fn performCorsPreflightRequest(
    allocator: Allocator,
    request: *InternalRequest,
) !PreflightResult {
    // Create preflight request
    const preflight_request = try createPreflightRequest(allocator, request);
    defer preflight_request.deinit();

    // Check cache first
    if (preflight_cache.lookup(request)) |cached| {
        return cached;
    }

    // Perform network request
    const backend_impl = try LibcurlBackend.init(allocator);
    defer backend_impl.deinit();

    const network_request = try buildNetworkRequest(allocator, preflight_request);
    defer freeNetworkRequest(allocator, network_request);

    var response = try backend_impl.asBackend().send(allocator, &network_request);
    defer response.deinit();

    // Validate preflight response
    const result = try validatePreflightResponse(response, request);

    // Cache successful result
    if (result.success) {
        try preflight_cache.store(request, result, result.max_age);
    }

    return result;
}
```

