## Overview
Implement thread safety enforcement for V8 integration including v8::Locker usage and thread affinity checks. Currently the code works correctly when used properly but has no safety rails to catch threading bugs.

## Problem Statement
**Current State**: 
- Thread-local storage used for context manager
- No v8::Locker enforcement
- No debug-mode thread affinity checks
- Relies on correct usage with no validation

**Research Requirement**: "Isolate-per-thread with v8::Locker for exclusive access"

**Impact**:
- Threading bugs cause undefined behavior/crashes
- Hard to debug cross-thread access
- No compile-time or runtime safety

## Research Document Requirements
From research.md Section 3.3.1 (Threading Model):
- V8 uses Isolate-per-thread with v8::Locker
- Each Isolate should only be accessed from one thread
- Need explicit locking for thread safety

## Implementation Requirements

### 1. Thread Affinity Tracking (Debug Mode)
Add to `v8_wrapper.cpp`:
```cpp
#include <thread>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <mutex>

#ifdef DEBUG
// Thread affinity tracking
static std::mutex g_affinity_mutex;
static std::unordered_map<Isolate*, std::thread::id> g_isolate_threads;

void checkThreadAffinity(Isolate* isolate, const char* operation) {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(g_affinity_mutex);

    auto tid = std::this_thread::get_id();
    auto it = g_isolate_threads.find(isolate);

    if (it != g_isolate_threads.end()) {
        if (it->second != tid) {
            // Thread affinity violation!
            std::ostringstream msg;
            msg << "FATAL: Isolate accessed from wrong thread!\n"
                << "  Operation: " << operation << "\n"
                << "  Expected thread: " << it->second << "\n"
                << "  Actual thread: " << tid << "\n"
                << "  Isolate: " << static_cast<void*>(isolate);

            fprintf(stderr, "%s\n", msg.str().c_str());
            abort();
        }
    } else {
        // First access - record thread
        g_isolate_threads[isolate] = tid;
    }
}

void clearThreadAffinity(Isolate* isolate) {
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(g_affinity_mutex);
    g_isolate_threads.erase(isolate);
}

#define CHECK_THREAD_AFFINITY(isolate, op) checkThreadAffinity(isolate, op)
#define CLEAR_THREAD_AFFINITY(isolate) clearThreadAffinity(isolate)

#else
#define CHECK_THREAD_AFFINITY(isolate, op) ((void)0)
#define CLEAR_THREAD_AFFINITY(isolate) ((void)0)
#endif
```

