## Overview

Fix `fromV8Value` in conversions.zig to create V8 Global handles when extracting function members from dictionaries.

## Root Cause \(conversions.zig:928-938\)

```zig
if \(T == *const anyopaque\) {
    // Comment says "Global\<Value\>*" but actually returns Local pointer\!
    return @ptrCast\(value\)\;
}
```

## Required Fix

```zig
if \(T == *const anyopaque\) {
    // Functions need Global handles to persist
    if \(v8.v8_Value_IsFunction\(value\)\) {
        const isolate = v8.v8_Isolate_GetCurrent\(\) orelse return @ptrCast\(value\)\;
        if \(v8.v8_Value_ToGlobal\(isolate, value\)\) \|global\| {
            return @ptrCast\(global\)\;
        }
    }
    return @ptrCast\(value\)\;
}
```

## Affected Dictionary Types

- UnderlyingSource \(start, pull, cancel\)
- UnderlyingSink \(start, write, close, abort\)
- Transformer \(start, transform, flush\)
- QueuingStrategy \(size\)

## Files to Modify

- `src/runtime/engines/v8/conversions.zig`

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Function values converted to Global handles
- [ ] Non-function values still work
- [ ] All stream callback extraction uses persistent handles

